                        "name": "Patrick Williams",
                        "email": "patrick@stwcx.xyz",
                        "username": "williamspatrick"
                    },
                    "message": "According to this https://systemd.io/ENVIRONMENT/ you've now set the timeout to be almost 2 years.  That might be a little excessive."
                },
                {
                    "file": "meta-facebook/meta-yosemite4/recipes-phosphor/sensors/dbus-sensors/yosemite4-dbus-timeout.conf",
                    "line": 2,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "Eric Yang",
                        "email": "eric.yang.wiwynn@gmail.com",
                        "username": "fornchu110"
                    },
                    "message": "Thank you for pointing this out.\nSorry for the confusion\u2014I had misunderstood and thought that the unit for SYSTEMD_BUS_TIMEOUT was microseconds, the same as sd_bus_set_method_call_timeout.\nI have now corrected it to SYSTEMD_BUS_TIMEOUT=60, as I intended to set it to 60 seconds."
                }
            ],
